cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Cite the ADIRO suite of ontologies as follows."
title: "ADIRO: AEC Drawing Information Representation Ontologies"
type: software
abstract: >-
  ADIRO (AEC Drawing Information Representation Ontologies) is a suite of OWL/TTL ontologies for representing
  drawings of the architecture, engineering and construction (AEC) domain: drawing metadata, common symbols,
  domain-common and domain-specific symbols, the geometry of what is found on a drawing, and the provenance and
  confidence of what is extracted from it. It supports machine-learning tasks, in particular information
  extraction, and lets drawings drive graph databases and knowledge graphs. Each module of the suite has its own
  IRI, version and documentation page.
